  "id": "bilateral-squat",
  "name": "Bilateral Squat",
  "definition": "A bilateral closed-chain compound squat in which both feet remain planted while the hips and knees flex to a reviewed thigh-parallel bottom position, then the athlete returns to standing through hip extension, knee extension, and ankle plantarflexion. The roster owns source-exact straight-bar back and front squats, a chest-held kettlebell goblet squat, and a vertical-rail Smith upper-back squat with zero horizontal foot offset. Each branch preserves its reported load position, grip, stance, and path instead of generalizing across squat fixtures. Vasti and gluteus maximus are the principal training emphases; rectus femoris, gastrocnemius, and soleus remain meaningful dynamic contributors, while the visible medial-hamstring region controls the hip, pelvis, and knee. Split-stance squats, lunges, step-ups, leg presses, hack and pendulum squats, belt squats, other Smith geometries, safety-bar and transformer-bar variants, box squats, heel-elevated squats, partial or full-depth squats, overhead squats, squat jumps, and thrusters remain outside this contract.",
